{"number":15,"title":"Matrices","slug":"matrices","color":"#16a34a","level":"","estTime":"","description":"Matrices — Class 10 Maths notes, solved examples, online MCQ test and IMO practice on Vidaara.","topics":[{"title":"Order of a Matrix","concept":"<p><strong>What is the order of a matrix?</strong> A <strong>matrix</strong> is a rectangular arrangement of numbers (called <strong>elements</strong>) arranged in rows and columns. The <strong>order</strong> of a matrix describes its size: <strong>number of rows × number of columns</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>Notation:</strong> A matrix with 'm' rows and 'n' columns has order <strong>m × n</strong> (read as \"m by n\").</p>\n<p><strong>Example:</strong> Matrix A = [ 3  5  7 ] has 1 row and 3 columns → order = 1 × 3 Matrix B = [ 2 ] has 1 row and 1 column → order = 1 × 1 Matrix C = [ 1  4 2  5 3  6 ] has 3 rows and 2 columns → order = 3 × 2</p>\n<p><strong>General representation:</strong> A = [aᵢⱼ] where:</p>\n<ul class=\"concept-list\"><li>i = row number (1 to m)</li><li>j = column number (1 to n)</li><li>aᵢⱼ = element in the i-th row and j-th column</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Special types of matrices based on order:</strong></p>\n<div style=\"overflow-x:auto\"><table class=\"concept-table\"><thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Definition</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Row matrix</td><td>m = 1 (one row)</td><td>[2, 5, 8]</td></tr><tr><td>Column matrix</td><td>n = 1 (one column)</td><td>[3; 7; 9]</td></tr><tr><td>Square matrix</td><td>m = n (same rows and columns)</td><td>[1 2; 3 4]</td></tr><tr><td>Zero matrix</td><td>All elements are 0</td><td>[0 0; 0 0]</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p><strong>Real-life analogy:</strong> Think of a matrix as a spreadsheet or a table. The order tells you how many rows and columns the table has — just like a classroom seating chart with 5 rows and 4 columns is a 5 × 4 arrangement!</p>","visual":"<div class=\"diagram-stack\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 560 250\" width=\"100%\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"c10c15t1a\">\n  <title id=\"c10c15t1a\">A 3 by 4 matrix with rows and columns labelled, showing order equals number of rows times number of columns</title>\n  <text x=\"280\" y=\"20\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14.5\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1e293b\">Order of a matrix = rows &#215; columns</text>\n  <path d=\"M150 48 L142 48 L142 198 L150 198\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#15803d\" stroke-width=\"2.2\"/>\n  <path d=\"M438 48 L446 48 L446 198 L438 198\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#15803d\" stroke-width=\"2.2\"/>\n  <text x=\"190\" y=\"80\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13.5\" fill=\"#1e293b\">a<tspan font-size=\"9\" dy=\"4\">11</tspan></text>\n  <text x=\"270\" y=\"80\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13.5\" fill=\"#1e293b\">a<tspan font-size=\"9\" dy=\"4\">12</tspan></text>\n  <text x=\"350\" y=\"80\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13.5\" fill=\"#1e293b\">a<tspan font-size=\"9\" dy=\"4\">13</tspan></text>\n  <text x=\"412\" y=\"80\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13.5\" fill=\"#1e293b\">a<tspan font-size=\"9\" dy=\"4\">14</tspan></text>\n  <text x=\"190\" y=\"128\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13.5\" fill=\"#1e293b\">a<tspan font-size=\"9\" dy=\"4\">21</tspan></text>\n  <text x=\"270\" y=\"128\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13.5\" fill=\"#1e293b\">a<tspan font-size=\"9\" dy=\"4\">22</tspan></text>\n  <text x=\"350\" y=\"128\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13.5\" fill=\"#1e293b\">a<tspan font-size=\"9\" dy=\"4\">23</tspan></text>\n  <text x=\"412\" y=\"128\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13.5\" fill=\"#1e293b\">a<tspan font-size=\"9\" dy=\"4\">24</tspan></text>\n  <text x=\"190\" y=\"176\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13.5\" fill=\"#1e293b\">a<tspan font-size=\"9\" dy=\"4\">31</tspan></text>\n  <text x=\"270\" y=\"176\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13.5\" fill=\"#1e293b\">a<tspan font-size=\"9\" dy=\"4\">32</tspan></text>\n  <text x=\"350\" y=\"176\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13.5\" fill=\"#1e293b\">a<tspan font-size=\"9\" dy=\"4\">33</tspan></text>\n  <text x=\"412\" y=\"176\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13.5\" fill=\"#1e293b\">a<tspan font-size=\"9\" dy=\"4\">34</tspan></text>\n  <text x=\"120\" y=\"80\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#475569\">row 1</text>\n  <text x=\"120\" y=\"128\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#475569\">row 2</text>\n  <text x=\"120\" y=\"176\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#475569\">row 3</text>\n  <text x=\"190\" y=\"42\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#15803d\" font-weight=\"700\">col 1</text>\n  <text x=\"270\" y=\"42\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#15803d\" font-weight=\"700\">col 2</text>\n  <text x=\"350\" y=\"42\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#15803d\" font-weight=\"700\">col 3</text>\n  <text x=\"412\" y=\"42\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#15803d\" font-weight=\"700\">col 4</text>\n  <text x=\"464\" y=\"128\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#475569\">3 rows</text>\n  <text x=\"280\" y=\"232\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12.5\" fill=\"#1e293b\">3 rows and 4 columns &#8594; order = 3 &#215; 4 (12 entries)</text>\n</svg>\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 560 185\" width=\"100%\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"c10c15t1b\">\n  <title id=\"c10c15t1b\">Mini grids of the special types of matrices: row, column, square, zero and identity</title>\n  <text x=\"280\" y=\"18\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14.5\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1e293b\">Special types of matrices</text>\n  <g>\n    <path d=\"M22 52 L17 52 L17 80 L22 80 M97 52 L102 52 L102 80 L97 80\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#1e293b\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/>\n    <rect x=\"24\" y=\"56\" width=\"22\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#eef2ff\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\"/>\n    <rect x=\"48\" y=\"56\" width=\"22\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#eef2ff\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\"/>\n    <rect x=\"72\" y=\"56\" width=\"22\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#eef2ff\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\"/>\n    <text x=\"59\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#475569\">Row (1&#215;3)</text>\n  </g>\n  <g>\n    <path d=\"M138 46 L133 46 L133 124 L138 124 M166 46 L171 46 L171 124 L166 124\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#1e293b\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/>\n    <rect x=\"140\" y=\"50\" width=\"24\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#dbeafe\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\"/>\n    <rect x=\"140\" y=\"74\" width=\"24\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#dbeafe\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\"/>\n    <rect x=\"140\" y=\"98\" width=\"24\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#dbeafe\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\"/>\n    <text x=\"152\" y=\"140\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#475569\">Column (3&#215;1)</text>\n  </g>\n  <g>\n    <path d=\"M214 52 L209 52 L209 102 L214 102 M268 52 L273 52 L273 102 L268 102\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#1e293b\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/>\n    <rect x=\"216\" y=\"56\" width=\"24\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f0fdf4\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\"/>\n    <rect x=\"242\" y=\"56\" width=\"24\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f0fdf4\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\"/>\n    <rect x=\"216\" y=\"78\" width=\"24\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f0fdf4\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\"/>\n    <rect x=\"242\" y=\"78\" width=\"24\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f0fdf4\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\"/>\n    <text x=\"241\" y=\"118\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#475569\">Square (2&#215;2)</text>\n  </g>\n  <g>\n    <path d=\"M314 52 L309 52 L309 102 L314 102 M368 52 L373 52 L373 102 L368 102\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#1e293b\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/>\n    <rect x=\"316\" y=\"56\" width=\"24\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#fef2f2\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\"/>\n    <rect x=\"342\" y=\"56\" width=\"24\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#fef2f2\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\"/>\n    <rect x=\"316\" y=\"78\" width=\"24\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#fef2f2\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\"/>\n    <rect x=\"342\" y=\"78\" width=\"24\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#fef2f2\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\"/>\n    <text x=\"328\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#94a3b8\">0</text>\n    <text x=\"354\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#94a3b8\">0</text>\n    <text x=\"328\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#94a3b8\">0</text>\n    <text x=\"354\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#94a3b8\">0</text>\n    <text x=\"341\" y=\"118\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#475569\">Zero (O)</text>\n  </g>\n  <g>\n    <path d=\"M428 52 L423 52 L423 102 L428 102 M482 52 L487 52 L487 102 L482 102\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#1e293b\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/>\n    <rect x=\"430\" y=\"56\" width=\"24\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#dbeafe\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\"/>\n    <rect x=\"456\" y=\"56\" width=\"24\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\"/>\n    <rect x=\"430\" y=\"78\" width=\"24\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#f1f5f9\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\"/>\n    <rect x=\"456\" y=\"78\" width=\"24\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#dbeafe\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\"/>\n    <text x=\"442\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#1d4ed8\" font-weight=\"700\">1</text>\n    <text x=\"468\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#94a3b8\">0</text>\n    <text x=\"442\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#94a3b8\">0</text>\n    <text x=\"468\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#1d4ed8\" font-weight=\"700\">1</text>\n    <text x=\"455\" y=\"118\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#475569\">Identity (I)</text>\n  </g>\n</svg>\n</div>","examples":[{"number":1,"problem":"Write the order of the following matrices:  \nA = [2 5 8 3], B = [1; 4; 7], C = [1 2; 3 4; 5 6]","solution":"<ol class=\"solution-steps\"><li>Step 1: Matrix A has 1 row and 4 columns → order = 1 × 4</li><li>Step 2: Matrix B has 3 rows and 1 column → order = 3 × 1</li><li>Step 3: Matrix C has 3 rows and 2 columns → order = 3 × 2</li></ol>\n<p class=\"solution-answer\"><strong>Answer:</strong> A: 1×4, B: 3×1, C: 3×2</p>"},{"number":2,"problem":"Construct a 2 × 3 matrix whose elements are given by aᵢⱼ = i + j.","solution":"<ol class=\"solution-steps\"><li>Step 1: Matrix has 2 rows and 3 columns</li><li>Step 2: For i=1, j=1: \\(a_{11}\\) = 1+1 = 2</li><li>Step 3: i=1, j=2: \\(a_{12}\\) = 1+2 = 3</li><li>Step 4: i=1, j=3: \\(a_{13}\\) = 1+3 = 4</li><li>Step 5: i=2, j=1: \\(a_{21}\\) = 2+1 = 3</li><li>Step 6: i=2, j=2: \\(a_{22}\\) = 2+2 = 4</li><li>Step 7: i=2, j=3: \\(a_{23}\\) = 2+3 = 5</li></ol>\n<p class=\"solution-answer\"><strong>Answer:</strong> A = [2 3 4; 3 4 5]</p>"},{"number":3,"problem":"If a matrix has 18 elements, what are the possible orders it can have?","solution":"<ol class=\"solution-steps\"><li>Step 1: Total elements = m × n = 18</li><li>Step 2: Find all pairs of positive integers (m, n) such that m × n = 18</li><li>Step 3: Factors of 18: 1×18, 2×9, 3×6, 6×3, 9×2, 18×1</li><li>Step 4: Each pair represents a possible order (m × n)</li></ol>\n<p class=\"solution-answer\"><strong>Answer:</strong> 1×18, 2×9, 3×6, 6×3, 9×2, 18×1</p>"}],"recap":["Order of a matrix = number of rows × number of columns","Rows are horizontal, columns are vertical","A matrix with m rows and n columns has order m × n","Row matrix: m = 1; Column matrix: n = 1","Square matrix: m = n","Element aᵢⱼ lies in i-th row and j-th column"],"quiz":[{"q":"The order of a matrix is written as:","options":["columns $\\times$ rows","rows $\\times$ columns","rows $+$ columns","rows $-$ columns"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Rows first, then columns."},{"q":"A $2\\times3$ matrix has how many elements?","options":["$5$","$6$","$23$","$1$"],"correct":1,"explanation":"$2\\times3=6$."},{"q":"A matrix with a single row is a:","options":["column matrix","row matrix","square matrix","zero matrix"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Row matrix."},{"q":"The order of $\\begin{bmatrix}1&2\\\\3&4\\end{bmatrix}$ is:","options":["$2\\times2$","$4\\times1$","$1\\times4$","$2\\times1$"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Two rows, two columns."}]},{"title":"Compatible Matrices","concept":"<p><strong>What are compatible matrices?</strong> Two matrices are said to be <strong>compatible</strong> for a given operation if their orders satisfy the conditions required for that operation. Compatibility depends on what operation we want to perform.</p>\n<p><strong>For addition and subtraction:</strong> Matrices must have the <strong>same order</strong>. You can only add or subtract matrices when they have exactly the same number of rows AND the same number of columns.</p>\n<p><strong>For multiplication (for your information — not in Grade 10 syllabus typically):</strong> The number of columns in the first matrix must equal the number of rows in the second matrix.</p>\n<p><strong>Real-life analogy:</strong> You can only add two tables if they have the same number of rows and columns (same layout). You can't add a 2×3 table to a 3×2 table because the positions don't match!</p>\n<p><strong>Examples of compatible matrices for addition:</strong></p>\n<div style=\"overflow-x:auto\"><table class=\"concept-table\"><thead><tr><th>Matrix A</th><th>Matrix B</th><th>Compatible?</th><th>Why?</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>2 × 3</td><td>2 × 3</td><td>✓ Yes</td><td>Same order</td></tr><tr><td>3 × 2</td><td>3 × 2</td><td>✓ Yes</td><td>Same order</td></tr><tr><td>2 × 3</td><td>3 × 2</td><td>✗ No</td><td>Different orders</td></tr><tr><td>1 × 4</td><td>1 × 4</td><td>✓ Yes</td><td>Same order</td></tr><tr><td>2 × 2</td><td>2 × 3</td><td>✗ No</td><td>Columns don't match</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","visual":"<div class=\"diagram-stack\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 560 230\" width=\"100%\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"c10c15t2a\">\n  <title id=\"c10c15t2a\">For addition the two matrices must have the same order; a 2 by 3 plus 2 by 3 is allowed but 2 by 3 plus 3 by 2 is not</title>\n  <text x=\"280\" y=\"20\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14.5\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1e293b\">Same order &#8594; can add or subtract</text>\n  <g>\n    <rect x=\"40\" y=\"44\" width=\"170\" height=\"120\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#f0fdf4\" stroke=\"#16a34a\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/>\n    <text x=\"125\" y=\"64\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12.5\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#15803d\">Compatible</text>\n    <path d=\"M66 78 L61 78 L61 128 L66 128 M124 78 L129 78 L129 128 L124 128\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#1e293b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n    <text x=\"80\" y=\"98\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#1e293b\">a</text>\n    <text x=\"110\" y=\"98\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#1e293b\">b</text>\n    <text x=\"80\" y=\"120\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#1e293b\">c</text>\n    <text x=\"110\" y=\"120\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#1e293b\">d</text>\n    <text x=\"142\" y=\"106\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#15803d\" font-weight=\"700\">+</text>\n    <path d=\"M158 78 L153 78 L153 128 L158 128 M192 78 L197 78 L197 128 L192 128\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#1e293b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n    <text x=\"170\" y=\"98\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#1e293b\">e</text>\n    <text x=\"170\" y=\"120\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#1e293b\">f</text>\n    <text x=\"183\" y=\"98\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#1e293b\">g</text>\n    <text x=\"183\" y=\"120\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#1e293b\">h</text>\n    <text x=\"125\" y=\"152\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11.5\" fill=\"#15803d\">2&#215;2 and 2&#215;2 &#8594; same order</text>\n  </g>\n  <g>\n    <rect x=\"350\" y=\"44\" width=\"170\" height=\"120\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fef2f2\" stroke=\"#dc2626\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/>\n    <text x=\"435\" y=\"64\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12.5\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#dc2626\">Not compatible</text>\n    <path d=\"M372 78 L367 78 L367 116 L372 116 M430 78 L435 78 L435 116 L430 116\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#1e293b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n    <text x=\"388\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#1e293b\">a</text>\n    <text x=\"414\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#1e293b\">b</text>\n    <text x=\"388\" y=\"110\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#1e293b\">c</text>\n    <text x=\"414\" y=\"110\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#1e293b\">d</text>\n    <text x=\"448\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#dc2626\" font-weight=\"700\">+</text>\n    <path d=\"M462 72 L457 72 L457 132 L462 132 M496 72 L501 72 L501 132 L496 132\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#1e293b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n    <text x=\"479\" y=\"88\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#1e293b\">p</text>\n    <text x=\"479\" y=\"106\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#1e293b\">q</text>\n    <text x=\"479\" y=\"124\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#1e293b\">r</text>\n    <text x=\"435\" y=\"152\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11.5\" fill=\"#dc2626\">2&#215;2 and 3&#215;1 &#8594; orders differ</text>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"280\" y=\"106\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#475569\">vs</text>\n  <text x=\"280\" y=\"196\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#475569\">Rule: A &#177; B is defined only when A and B have the SAME order.</text>\n  <text x=\"280\" y=\"216\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11.5\" fill=\"#475569\">(For a product AB: columns of A must equal rows of B.)</text>\n</svg>\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 560 175\" width=\"100%\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"c10c15t2b\">\n  <title id=\"c10c15t2b\">Matrix equality: two matrices are equal when they have the same order and every corresponding entry is equal</title>\n  <text x=\"280\" y=\"20\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14.5\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1e293b\">Equality: same order AND matching entries</text>\n  <path d=\"M120 46 L115 46 L115 116 L120 116 M196 46 L201 46 L201 116 L196 116\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#1e293b\" stroke-width=\"1.7\"/>\n  <text x=\"140\" y=\"74\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\">x+y</text>\n  <text x=\"178\" y=\"74\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\">2</text>\n  <text x=\"140\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\">5</text>\n  <text x=\"178\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\">x&#8722;y</text>\n  <text x=\"225\" y=\"86\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#15803d\" font-weight=\"700\">=</text>\n  <path d=\"M256 46 L251 46 L251 116 L256 116 M332 46 L337 46 L337 116 L332 116\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#1e293b\" stroke-width=\"1.7\"/>\n  <text x=\"276\" y=\"74\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\">7</text>\n  <text x=\"314\" y=\"74\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\">2</text>\n  <text x=\"276\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\">5</text>\n  <text x=\"314\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\">3</text>\n  <line x1=\"345\" y1=\"86\" x2=\"380\" y2=\"86\" stroke=\"#475569\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 3\"/>\n  <text x=\"386\" y=\"76\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#475569\">x + y = 7</text>\n  <text x=\"386\" y=\"98\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#475569\">x &#8722; y = 3</text>\n  <text x=\"280\" y=\"146\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#1e293b\">Equate corresponding entries &#8594; solve: x = 5, y = 2</text>\n  <text x=\"280\" y=\"166\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11.5\" fill=\"#475569\">One matrix equation becomes a set of scalar equations.</text>\n</svg>\n</div>","examples":[{"number":1,"problem":"Check whether the following pairs of matrices are compatible for addition:  \n(i) A = 2×3, B = 2×3 (ii) P = 3×2, Q = 2×3 (iii) X = 1×4, Y = 1×4","solution":"<ol class=\"solution-steps\"><li>Step 1: For addition, matrices must have the same order</li><li>Step 2: (i) A is 2×3, B is 2×3 → same order → compatible</li><li>Step 3: (ii) P is 3×2, Q is 2×3 → different orders → not compatible</li><li>Step 4: (iii) X is 1×4, Y is 1×4 → same order → compatible</li></ol>\n<p class=\"solution-answer\"><strong>Answer:</strong> (i) Yes, (ii) No, (iii) Yes</p>"},{"number":2,"problem":"Can we add a 3×4 matrix and a 3×4 matrix? What about a 3×4 and a 4×3?","solution":"<ol class=\"solution-steps\"><li>Step 1: First pair: 3×4 and 3×4 → same order (both 3 rows, 4 columns)</li><li>Step 2: Therefore, they ARE compatible for addition</li><li>Step 3: Second pair: 3×4 and 4×3 → different orders</li><li>Step 4: 3×4 has 3 rows, 4×3 has 4 rows → not compatible</li></ol>\n<p class=\"solution-answer\"><strong>Answer:</strong> 3×4 and 3×4: Yes; 3×4 and 4×3: No</p>"},{"number":3,"problem":"If matrix A is of order 2×3 and A + B is defined, what can you say about the order of B?","solution":"<ol class=\"solution-steps\"><li>Step 1: For A + B to be defined, A and B must have the same order</li><li>Step 2: A has order 2×3 (2 rows, 3 columns)</li><li>Step 3: Therefore, B must also have order 2×3</li></ol>\n<p class=\"solution-answer\"><strong>Answer:</strong> B must be of order 2×3</p>"}],"recap":["For addition/subtraction, matrices must have the <strong>same order</strong>","Compatible means the operation is possible (defined)","If orders are different, addition/subtraction is NOT possible","A + B = B + A (commutative property holds for addition)","(A + B) + C = A + (B + C) (associative property holds)","Zero matrix (same order) is the additive identity"],"quiz":[{"q":"Two matrices can be added if they have the:","options":["same number of rows only","same order","same first element","product defined"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Same order for addition."},{"q":"For the product $AB$ to exist:","options":["rows of $A$ $=$ rows of $B$","columns of $A$ $=$ rows of $B$","$A=B$","both are square"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Inner dimensions match."},{"q":"A $2\\times3$ matrix and a $3\\times2$ matrix can be:","options":["added","multiplied","neither","subtracted"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Multiplication is defined."},{"q":"Equal matrices have the same order and:","options":["equal corresponding entries","equal sums","equal first row","equal determinant only"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Entry-by-entry equal."}]},{"title":"Addition and Subtraction of Matrices, and Multiplication by a Scalar","concept":"<p><strong>What is matrix addition and subtraction?</strong> When two matrices have the same order, we can <strong>add</strong> or <strong>subtract</strong> them by adding or subtracting the corresponding elements (elements in the same position).</p>\n<p><strong>Addition:</strong> If A = [aᵢⱼ] and B = [bᵢⱼ] are both m × n matrices, then: <strong>A + B = [aᵢⱼ + bᵢⱼ]</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Subtraction:</strong> <strong>A − B = [aᵢⱼ − bᵢⱼ]</strong></p>\n<p><strong>What is scalar multiplication?</strong> <strong>Scalar multiplication</strong> means multiplying every element of a matrix by the same number (called a <strong>scalar</strong>). If k is a scalar and A = [aᵢⱼ], then: <strong>kA = [k × aᵢⱼ]</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Properties of scalar multiplication:</strong></p>\n<ul class=\"concept-list\"><li>k(A + B) = kA + kB (distributive)</li><li>(k + m)A = kA + mA (distributive)</li><li>k(mA) = (km)A (associative)</li><li>1 × A = A (identity)</li><li>0 × A = Zero matrix</li></ul>\n<p><strong>Real-life analogy:</strong> If matrix A represents the prices of items in two stores, and matrix B represents a price increase, then A + B gives the new prices. Scalar multiplication is like applying a 10% discount (multiply by 0.9) to all prices at once!</p>","visual":"<div class=\"diagram-stack\">\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 560 200\" width=\"100%\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"c10c15t3a\">\n  <title id=\"c10c15t3a\">Matrix addition done element by element on two 2 by 2 matrices, adding entries in the same position</title>\n  <text x=\"280\" y=\"20\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14.5\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1e293b\">Addition: add entries in the same position</text>\n  <path d=\"M40 46 L35 46 L35 120 L40 120 M118 46 L123 46 L123 120 L118 120\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#1e293b\" stroke-width=\"1.7\"/>\n  <text x=\"60\" y=\"76\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\">a</text>\n  <text x=\"98\" y=\"76\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\">b</text>\n  <text x=\"60\" y=\"104\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\">c</text>\n  <text x=\"98\" y=\"104\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\">d</text>\n  <text x=\"143\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#15803d\" font-weight=\"700\">+</text>\n  <path d=\"M168 46 L163 46 L163 120 L168 120 M246 46 L251 46 L251 120 L246 120\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#1e293b\" stroke-width=\"1.7\"/>\n  <text x=\"188\" y=\"76\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\">e</text>\n  <text x=\"226\" y=\"76\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\">f</text>\n  <text x=\"188\" y=\"104\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\">g</text>\n  <text x=\"226\" y=\"104\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\">h</text>\n  <text x=\"271\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#15803d\" font-weight=\"700\">=</text>\n  <path d=\"M296 46 L291 46 L291 120 L296 120 M520 46 L525 46 L525 120 L520 120\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#15803d\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <rect x=\"304\" y=\"54\" width=\"96\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#f0fdf4\" stroke=\"#16a34a\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/>\n  <rect x=\"408\" y=\"54\" width=\"96\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#f0fdf4\" stroke=\"#16a34a\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/>\n  <rect x=\"304\" y=\"86\" width=\"96\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#f0fdf4\" stroke=\"#16a34a\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/>\n  <rect x=\"408\" y=\"86\" width=\"96\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#f0fdf4\" stroke=\"#16a34a\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/>\n  <text x=\"352\" y=\"72\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12.5\" fill=\"#15803d\" font-weight=\"700\">a+e</text>\n  <text x=\"456\" y=\"72\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12.5\" fill=\"#15803d\" font-weight=\"700\">b+f</text>\n  <text x=\"352\" y=\"104\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12.5\" fill=\"#15803d\" font-weight=\"700\">c+g</text>\n  <text x=\"456\" y=\"104\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12.5\" fill=\"#15803d\" font-weight=\"700\">d+h</text>\n  <text x=\"280\" y=\"150\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#1e293b\">Example: [1 2; 3 4] + [5 6; 7 8] = [6 8; 10 12]</text>\n  <text x=\"280\" y=\"174\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11.5\" fill=\"#475569\">Subtraction works the same way: subtract corresponding entries.</text>\n</svg>\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 560 185\" width=\"100%\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"c10c15t3b\">\n  <title id=\"c10c15t3b\">Scalar multiplication multiplies every entry of the matrix by the scalar k</title>\n  <text x=\"280\" y=\"20\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"14.5\" font-weight=\"700\" fill=\"#1e293b\">Scalar multiplication: k multiplies every entry</text>\n  <text x=\"60\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"20\" fill=\"#b45309\" font-weight=\"700\">k</text>\n  <text x=\"60\" y=\"112\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#b45309\">scalar</text>\n  <path d=\"M96 50 L91 50 L91 124 L96 124 M174 50 L179 50 L179 124 L174 124\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#1e293b\" stroke-width=\"1.7\"/>\n  <text x=\"116\" y=\"80\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\">a</text>\n  <text x=\"154\" y=\"80\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\">b</text>\n  <text x=\"116\" y=\"108\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\">c</text>\n  <text x=\"154\" y=\"108\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\">d</text>\n  <text x=\"204\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#b45309\" font-weight=\"700\">=</text>\n  <path d=\"M232 50 L227 50 L227 124 L232 124 M520 50 L525 50 L525 124 L520 124\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#b45309\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <rect x=\"242\" y=\"58\" width=\"124\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#fff7ed\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/>\n  <rect x=\"374\" y=\"58\" width=\"124\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#fff7ed\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/>\n  <rect x=\"242\" y=\"90\" width=\"124\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#fff7ed\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/>\n  <rect x=\"374\" y=\"90\" width=\"124\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#fff7ed\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/>\n  <text x=\"304\" y=\"76\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12.5\" fill=\"#b45309\" font-weight=\"700\">k&#183;a</text>\n  <text x=\"436\" y=\"76\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12.5\" fill=\"#b45309\" font-weight=\"700\">k&#183;b</text>\n  <text x=\"304\" y=\"108\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12.5\" fill=\"#b45309\" font-weight=\"700\">k&#183;c</text>\n  <text x=\"436\" y=\"108\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12.5\" fill=\"#b45309\" font-weight=\"700\">k&#183;d</text>\n  <text x=\"280\" y=\"156\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#1e293b\">Example: 3 &#183; [1 2; 3 4] = [3 6; 9 12]</text>\n  <text x=\"280\" y=\"176\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11.5\" fill=\"#475569\">Order is unchanged; only the entries are scaled.</text>\n</svg>\n</div>","examples":[{"number":1,"problem":"If A = [1 2; 3 4] and B = [5 6; 7 8], find A + B and A − B.","solution":"<ol class=\"solution-steps\"><li>Step 1: A + B = [1+5, 2+6; 3+7, 4+8] = [6, 8; 10, 12]</li><li>Step 2: A − B = [1−5, 2−6; 3−7, 4−8] = [−4, −4; −4, −4]</li></ol>\n<p class=\"solution-answer\"><strong>Answer:</strong> A + B = [6 8; 10 12]; A − B = [−4 −4; −4 −4]</p>"},{"number":2,"problem":"Given A = [2 4; 6 8], find 5A.","solution":"<ol class=\"solution-steps\"><li>Step 1: Multiply each element by 5: 5×2 = 10, 5×4 = 20, 5×6 = 30, 5×8 = 40</li></ol>\n<p class=\"solution-answer\"><strong>Answer:</strong> 5A = [10 20; 30 40]</p>"},{"number":3,"problem":"If A = [3 1; 2 4] and B = [2 3; 1 5], find 3A − 2B.","solution":"<ol class=\"solution-steps\"><li>Step 1: 3A = [9 3; 6 12]</li><li>Step 2: 2B = [4 6; 2 10]</li><li>Step 3: 3A − 2B = [9−4, 3−6; 6−2, 12−10] = [5, −3; 4, 2]</li></ol>\n<p class=\"solution-answer\"><strong>Answer:</strong> 3A − 2B = [5 −3; 4 2]</p>"}],"recap":["Addition/subtraction only possible for matrices of same order","Add/subtract corresponding elements (same row, same column)","Scalar multiplication multiplies EVERY element by the scalar","Scalar multiplication is distributive over addition","Zero matrix (all zeros) is the additive identity","Order remains the same after addition, subtraction, and scalar multiplication"],"quiz":[{"q":"Matrices are added:","options":["row by column","element by element","by determinants","by transposing"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Add corresponding entries."},{"q":"Scalar multiplication multiplies:","options":["only the diagonal","every element","the first row","nothing"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Each entry by the scalar."},{"q":"$2\\begin{bmatrix}1&2\\\\3&4\\end{bmatrix}=$","options":["$\\begin{bmatrix}2&4\\\\6&8\\end{bmatrix}$","$\\begin{bmatrix}1&2\\\\3&4\\end{bmatrix}$","$\\begin{bmatrix}2&2\\\\2&2\\end{bmatrix}$","$\\begin{bmatrix}3&4\\\\5&6\\end{bmatrix}$"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Double each entry."},{"q":"$A-A=$","options":["$A$","the zero matrix","$2A$","the identity"],"correct":1,"explanation":"All entries become $0$."}]}],"tests":{"online":{"title":"Online Test — Matrices","minutes":15,"questions":[{"q":"The order of matrix [1 2 3; 4 5 6] is:","options":["2×2","2×3","3×2","3×3"],"correct":1,"explanation":"2 rows, 3 columns → 2×3","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"A matrix with 3 rows and 1 column is called a:","options":["Row matrix","Column matrix","Square matrix","Zero matrix"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Column matrix has n=1","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"Which of the following pairs can be added?","options":["2×3 and 2×3","2×3 and 3×2","3×1 and 1×3","2×2 and 3×3"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Addition requires same order","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"If A = [1 2; 3 4], then 2A = ?","options":["[2 4; 6 8]","[1 2; 3 4]","[2 4; 3 4]","[1 4; 6 8]"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Multiply each element by 2","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"A scalar is a:","options":["Matrix","Number","Vector","Row"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Scalar = ordinary number","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"For matrix addition, which property holds?","options":["A+B = B+A","A+B ≠ B+A","A+B is undefined","A+B = A"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Addition is commutative","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"If A = [3 5; 2 7] and B = [1 4; 6 8], find A − B","options":["[2 1; -4 -1]","[4 9; 8 15]","[2 -1; 4 1]","[2 9; -4 -1]"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Subtract entrywise: 3-1=2, 5-4=1, 2-6=-4, 7-8=-1, giving [2 1; -4 -1].","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"A 2×3 matrix has how many elements?","options":["5","6","8","12"],"correct":1,"explanation":"2×3 = 6 elements","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"If A is a 3×4 matrix, then 5A has order:","options":["3×4","4×3","15×20","3×20"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Scalar multiplication doesn't change order","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"Which matrix is the additive identity?","options":["[1]","[0]","[1 0; 0 1]","[0 0; 0 0]"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Zero matrix (all zeros)","difficulty":"medium"}]},"imo":{"title":"IMO Practice — Matrices","minutes":15,"questions":[{"q":"Find x and y if [x+y, x-y; 2, 3] = [6, 2; 2, 3]","options":["x=4,y=2","x=2,y=4","x=4,y=-2","x=3,y=3"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Equating entries: x+y=6 and x-y=2. Adding gives 2x=8, so x=4 and y=2.","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"If 2[3 4; 5 6] + 3[1 2; 3 4] = [a b; c d], find a+b+c+d","options":["44","48","52","66"],"correct":3,"explanation":"2A = [6 8; 10 12] and 3B = [3 6; 9 12], so the sum is [9 14; 19 24]. Then a+b+c+d = 9+14+19+24 = 66.","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"If A = [1 2; 3 4] and B = [2 0; 1 2], find the matrix X such that 2X + A = B","options":["[0.5 -1; -1 -1]","[0.5 1; -1 1]","[-0.5 -1; 1 -1]","[0.5 1; -1 -1]"],"correct":0,"explanation":"From 2X + A = B, 2X = B - A = [1 -2; -2 -2], so X = [0.5 -1; -1 -1].","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"For what value of k does k[2 4; 6 8] = [6 12; 18 24]?","options":["2","3","4","5"],"correct":1,"explanation":"k×2=6→k=3; also 3×4=12, 3×6=18, 3×8=24 ✓","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"If A = [1 2; 3 4], B = [5 6; 7 8], then (A+B) − (A−B) = ?","options":["B","2B","2A","Zero matrix"],"correct":1,"explanation":"(A+B)-(A-B)=A+B-A+B=2B","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"Find the value of a and b if [a+b, a-b; 4, 6] = [8, 2; 4, 6]","options":["a=5,b=3","a=3,b=5","a=5,b=-3","a=6,b=2"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Equating entries: a+b=8 and a-b=2. Adding gives 2a=10, so a=5 and b=3.","difficulty":"medium"}]}}}